# The Fedora half of this module's one line. The daemon is the base's —
# `openssh-server` is in `quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc:44` and
# `assets/bases.kdl` says so with `provides "ssh"` — and the
# enablement is this module's, the same split the `deb/` copy describes.
#
# The unit is `sshd.service` here and `ssh.service` on the deb families, which
# is the whole reason this is a family directory: a preset is applied line by
# line and a line naming a unit that does not exist fails the build, so one
# file could not say both.
#
# Fedora's own `90-default.preset` already enables it, so on this family the
# line changes nothing about the built image. It is here because the module's
# claim is that *it* opens ssh: an image that gets the daemon enabled only
# because the distro's default preset happened to say so has no way to notice
# when that changes, and `45-` is read before `90-` either way.
enable sshd.service
